> Iris: residual noise at the least-squares solution

Predict Petal.Length from Sepal.Length, Sepal.Width and Petal.Width, including
an intercept, on the 150 Iris flowers. Measurements stay in centimetres without
standardisation. Formula freezes the complete numeric design, and the direct
linear-model fit supplies an independent algebraic least-squares control.
The Species summary describes these observations; Species is not a predictor.
This is training-loss minimisation, not a claim about held-out predictive accuracy.

Use eta=.01, seed 42 and zero tolerance. SGD uses 300 epochs, SVRG 100 epochs
of n inner steps, and SAGA 45000 updates. Count the initial SAGA table, all SVRG
snapshots and both of its inner gradient requests. The plotted reference is the
linear-model RSS/2 at full-sum scale. Compare coefficient error and full gradient
norm as well as the loss gap: an ill-conditioned direction can remain inaccurate
while changing the loss little. No winner is claimed across tuned rates or budgets.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_variance_iris.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o                 = dm::optim;
  const auto          iris    = dm::datasets::iris();
  const std::string   formula = "Petal.Length ~ Sepal.Length + Sepal.Width + Petal.Width";
  auto                f       = o::LeastSquaresObjective::from_data(iris, formula);
  const dm::stats::LM ref(iris, formula);
  const double        minimum = ref.rss() / 2;
  o::SGDOptions       a;
  a.step_size  = .01;
  a.max_epochs = 300;
  a.tolerance  = 0;
  o::SVRGOptions b;
  b.step_size  = .01;
  b.max_epochs = 100;
  b.tolerance  = 0;
  o::SAGAOptions c;
  c.step_size      = .01;
  c.max_iterations = 45000;
  c.tolerance      = 0;
  const std::vector<double>       start(4, 0);
  std::vector<o::OptimizationRun> runs{
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableSeparableFunction>(f, o::SGD(a), start),
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableSeparableFunction>(f, o::SVRG(b), start),
      o::trace_optimize<o::DifferentiableSeparableFunction>(f, o::SAGA(c), start)};
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"SGD", "SVRG", "SAGA"};
  o::optimization_comparison(f, runs, names, "value", minimum, false, true)
      .title("Iris: residual noise and nominal gradient work")
      .size(850, 490)
      .save_svg("build/opt_variance_iris.svg");
  std::print(
      "{}\n\nDirect least squares f={:.10g}, mean-loss L={:.8g}.\n",
      (iris | dm::group_by("Species") |
       dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("n"), dm::agg::mean("Petal.Length", "mean_length_cm")))
          .to_md(4),
      minimum,
      f.mean_loss_lipschitz());
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < runs.size(); ++i) {
    double e = 0;
    for (std::size_t j = 0; j < 4; ++j)
      e = std::max(e, std::abs(runs[i].coordinates[j] - ref.coefficients()[j]));
    std::print(
        "{}: max coefficient error={:.8g}\n\n{}\n\n{}\n\n",
        names[i],
        e,
        runs[i].summary().to_md(8),
        runs[i].trace.counts().to_md(0));
  }
}
```
